.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd July 31, 2026
.Dt NOTIFYCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm notifyctl
.Nd validate and operate the NotifyCmp service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm configtest
.Op Ar file
.Nm
.Cm publish
.Ar topic
.Op Ar payload
.Nm
.Cm state-get
.Ar topic
.Nm
.Cm state-set
.Ar topic value
.Nm
.Cm watch
.Ar topic
.Op Ar timeout-ms
.Nm
.Cm stats
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the administrator and diagnostic client for
.Xr bsdnotify 8 .
It uses
.Xr libnotifycmp 3
for all live service operations and is therefore subject to the immutable
serviced identity policy of the invoking service.
It receives no implicit administrative bypass.
.Pp
The
.Cm configtest
command parses the supplied policy file, or
.Pa /etc/bsdnotify.conf
by default, with the same strict parser used by the daemon.
It does not modify or reload the running service.
.Cm publish ,
.Cm state-get ,
.Cm state-set ,
.Cm watch ,
and
.Cm stats
provide bounded diagnostic access to the corresponding public API.
Payload output is written as opaque bytes after one metadata line.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libnotifycmp 3 ,
.Xr bsdnotify 8 ,
.Xr serviced 8
